#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:4
msgid "構造最適化"
msgstr "Structure Optimization"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:6
msgid ""
"構造最適化は、原子の位置やセルを動かし、指定した条件のもとで エネルギーが低くなる構造を求める計算である。原子に働く力は位置を動かす "
"手がかりになり、セルに生じる応力は格子の形や体積を変える手がかりになる。 どの自由度を動かすかによって、得られる構造の意味が変わる。"
msgstr ""
"Structure optimization finds a lower-energy structure under specified "
"conditions by moving atoms, changing the cell, or both. The forces on the"
" atoms tell us how to move them, and the stress in the cell tells us how "
"to change the shape or volume of the lattice. The meaning of the "
"resulting structure depends on which degrees of freedom are allowed to "
"change."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:11
msgid ""
"前提は\\ :ref:`格子ベクトルの独立な成分<lattice-dof>`\\ と :ref:`構造ごとの電子状態計算<kohn-sham-"
"dft>`\\ である。 単点計算、固定セル緩和、可変セル最適化を使い分け、結果の収束を判断する。"
msgstr ""
"This article assumes familiarity with the \\ :ref:`independent components"
" of lattice vectors <lattice-dof>`\\  and with :ref:`electronic structure"
" calculations for a given structure <kohn-sham-dft>`\\ . It explains when"
" to use single-point calculations, fixed-cell relaxation, or variable-"
"cell optimization, and how to judge convergence."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:16
msgid "単点計算と固定セル緩和"
msgstr "Single-Point Calculations and Fixed-Cell Relaxation"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:18
msgid ""
"**単点計算** では、セルも原子座標も固定し、その構造でエネルギーや力などを 求める。特定の原子を少しずつずらしてエネルギー曲線を作る場合、 "
"各点の変位を保つために単点計算を使う。変位させるたびに同じ極小へ緩和すると、 指定した変位におけるエネルギーが得られなくなる。"
msgstr ""
"A **single-point calculation** keeps the cell and atomic coordinates "
"fixed and evaluates quantities such as the energy and forces at that "
"structure. To construct an energy curve by moving selected atoms in small"
" increments, use a single-point calculation to preserve the displacement "
"at each point. If each displaced structure relaxes to the same minimum, "
"the energies at the specified displacements are lost."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:23
msgid ""
"**固定セル緩和** では、セルの大きさと形を固定し、原子位置を動かす。 原子配置のエネルギーを :math:`E`、原子 :math:`i` "
"の位置を :math:`\\boldsymbol r_i`、セルを表す格子行列を :math:`A` とする。 力 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol F_i` と位置の微小変化 :math:`\\delta\\boldsymbol r_i` "
"に対するエネルギー変化は"
msgstr ""
"In **fixed-cell relaxation**, the size and shape of the cell stay fixed "
"while the atomic positions can change. Let :math:`E` be the energy of the"
" atomic configuration, :math:`i` the atom index, :math:`\\boldsymbol r_i`"
" its position, and :math:`A` the lattice matrix specifying the cell. The "
"force :math:`\\boldsymbol F_i` and the energy change for a small "
"displacement :math:`\\delta\\boldsymbol r_i` are given by"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\left.\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial\\boldsymbol "
"r_i}\\right|_A,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\delta E=-\\sum_i\\boldsymbol F_i\\cdot\\delta\\boldsymbol r_i"
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol F_i=-\\left.\\frac{\\partial E}{\\partial\\boldsymbol "
"r_i}\\right|_A,\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\delta E=-\\sum_i\\boldsymbol F_i\\cdot\\delta\\boldsymbol r_i"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:36
msgid ""
"となる。力の方向へ十分小さく動かすと、一次のエネルギー変化は負になる。 指定した方向だけを動かすときは、その方向への力の成分を用いる。 "
"緩和後に応力が残っていれば、固定したセルを変えたときにエネルギーが まだ変わることを示す。"
msgstr ""
"A sufficiently small displacement along the force gives a negative first-"
"order energy change. If motion is allowed only in a specified direction, "
"use the component of the force along that direction. Residual stress "
"after relaxation shows that the energy still changes if the fixed cell is"
" allowed to change."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:41
msgid ""
"スメアリングを使う電子状態計算では、 :ref:`力と応力に対応する自由エネルギー<smearing-and-free-energy>`\\ を "
"最小化する。以降の :math:`E` は、最適化に用いるエネルギーを表す。"
msgstr ""
"Electronic structure calculations with smearing minimize the :ref:`free "
"energy associated with the forces and stress <smearing-and-free-"
"energy>`\\ . Hereafter :math:`E` denotes the energy used in the "
"optimization."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:48
msgid "可変セル最適化と外圧"
msgstr "Variable-Cell Optimization and External Pressure"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:50
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**可変セル最適化** では、セルの形や大きさを変える。内部座標も自由に した場合は、セルの変形に伴って原子位置も緩和する。体積を "
":math:`V`、 セルの微小な対称ひずみを :math:`\\delta\\varepsilon_{ab}` とする。 "
"原子の分率座標を固定したセル変形でのエネルギー変化を、引張を正とした 応力 :math:`\\sigma_{ab}` を用いて書くと "
"[OptNielsenMartin1985]_、"
msgstr ""
"**Variable-cell optimization** varies the shape or size of the cell. If "
"the internal coordinates are also free, the atomic positions relax as the"
" cell deforms. Let :math:`V` be the volume and "
":math:`\\delta\\varepsilon_{ab}` an infinitesimal symmetric strain of the"
" cell. With the fractional coordinates of the atoms held fixed and "
"tensile stress taken as positive, the stress :math:`\\sigma_{ab}` gives "
"the energy change for a cell deformation as follows "
"[OptNielsenMartin1985]_"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:56
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\delta E=V\\sum_{a,b}\\sigma_{ab}\\,\\delta\\varepsilon_{ab},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\delta V=V\\sum_a\\delta\\varepsilon_{aa}"
msgstr ""
"\\delta E=V\\sum_{a,b}\\sigma_{ab}\\,\\delta\\varepsilon_{ab},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\delta V=V\\sum_a\\delta\\varepsilon_{aa}"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:63
msgid ""
"となる。ここで :math:`a,b` は直交座標の成分で、対称なテンソルの 両方の添字について和を取る。体積の式は、ひずみの一次では "
"セルを変形する行列の行列式の変化が対角成分の和になることから得られる。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`a,b` index Cartesian components, and the sum runs over both "
"indices of the symmetric tensors. The volume expression follows because, "
"to first order in strain, the change in the determinant of the matrix "
"that deforms the cell equals the sum of the diagonal strain components."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:67
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"一定の静水圧 :math:`P_{\\rm ext}` のもとでは、:math:`H=E+P_{\\rm ext}V` を最小化する。:eq"
":`structure-stress-variation`\\ の二式を代入すると、 セル変形に対する :math:`H` の変化は"
msgstr ""
"At constant hydrostatic pressure :math:`P_{\\rm ext}`, minimize "
":math:`H=E+P_{\\rm ext}V`. Substituting the two expressions from Equation"
" :eq:`structure-stress-variation`\\  gives the change in :math:`H` under "
"cell deformation,"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:71
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\delta H\n"
"  = V\\sum_{a,b}(\\sigma_{ab}+P_{\\rm ext}\\delta_{ab})\\,\n"
"     \\delta\\varepsilon_{ab}"
msgstr ""
"\\delta H\n"
"  = V\\sum_{a,b}(\\sigma_{ab}+P_{\\rm ext}\\delta_{ab})\\,\n"
"     \\delta\\varepsilon_{ab}"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:78
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"となる。:math:`\\delta_{ab}` は :math:`a=b` で1、それ以外で0である。 "
"セルのひずみがすべて自由なら、収束時の内部応力は外圧とつり合い、 :math:`\\sigma_{ab}=-P_{\\rm "
"ext}\\delta_{ab}` になる。 許すセル変形を限定すると、その変形方向の成分だけが収束の判定に入る。 圧縮を正とした内部圧力は "
":math:`P=-\\operatorname{tr}(\\sigma)/3` である。 "
"プログラムが圧縮を正とする符号で応力成分を出す場合、ここで使う 引張を正とした成分とは符号が逆になる。外圧との差を調べる前に、 "
"出力の対角成分と圧力の符号をこの関係でそろえる。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`\\delta_{ab}` is 1 if :math:`a=b` and 0 otherwise. If all "
"cell strains are free, the internal stress balances the external pressure"
" at convergence, giving :math:`\\sigma_{ab}=-P_{\\rm ext}\\delta_{ab}`. "
"If cell deformation is restricted, only the components along the allowed "
"deformation directions enter the convergence criterion. With compression "
"taken as positive, the internal pressure is "
":math:`P=-\\operatorname{tr}(\\sigma)/3`. If a program reports stress "
"components with compression positive, their signs are opposite to the "
"tension-positive components used here. Use this relationship to put the "
"reported diagonal components and the pressure in a consistent sign "
"convention before comparing with the external pressure."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:90
msgid "対称性を保つ格子と原子座標の拘束"
msgstr "Symmetry-Preserving Constraints on the Lattice and Atomic Coordinates"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:92
msgid ""
"各相を同じ条件で比較したいときは、想定する相の格子を保つように セルの自由度を選ぶ。次の表は、辺の長さ :math:`a,b,c` と格子角 "
":math:`\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma` を使った典型的な設定である。菱面体格子は 菱面体軸を選んだ場合を示す。"
msgstr ""
"To compare phases under the same conditions, choose cell degrees of "
"freedom that preserve the lattice shape of each phase under "
"consideration. The table shows typical constraints in terms of the edge "
"lengths :math:`a,b,c` and lattice angles :math:`\\alpha,\\beta,\\gamma`. "
"The rhombohedral case uses rhombohedral axes."

