#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:115
msgid "共通の辺長と角度"
msgstr "Common edge length and angle"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:117
msgid ""
"格子の条件はセルの形を定める。結晶全体の対称性は原子配置にも依存するので、 相の対称性を保つには、等価な原子同士の関係が保たれるように内部座標の "
"自由度も選ぶ。分率座標を固定してセルを変える場合、原子の絶対位置は セルとともに動く。こうした計算は、格子の変化と内部座標の緩和の影響を "
"切り分けるときに使える。"
msgstr ""
"Lattice constraints determine the cell shape. Because the symmetry of the"
" crystal as a whole also depends on the atomic configuration, choose the "
"internal degrees of freedom so that the relations between equivalent "
"atoms are preserved. When the cell changes at fixed fractional "
"coordinates, the absolute atomic positions move with the cell. Such "
"calculations can isolate the effect of changing the lattice from the "
"effect of relaxing the internal coordinates."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:123
msgid ""
"`BaTiO₃の格子定数 <https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/lattice-"
"constant.html>`__ と `安定基底状態 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/stability.html>`__ "
"では、相ごとの格子を求めた後、その格子を固定して原子座標を緩和している。 この順序で計算すると、指定した格子上での相対エネルギーを比較できる。 "
"セルと原子座標の変化が強く結び付く場合は、両方の自由度を許したときに 結果がどう変わるかも調べられる。"
msgstr ""
"In the calculation examples `Lattice Constants of BaTiO₃ <https://example"
".quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/lattice-constant.html>`__ and `Stable "
"Ground State of BaTiO₃ <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/stability.html>`__, the lattice of each phase "
"is determined first and its atomic coordinates are then relaxed with that"
" lattice held fixed. This sequence permits comparing relative energies at"
" the specified lattices. When changes in the cell and atomic coordinates "
"are strongly coupled, one can also examine how the results change when "
"both sets of degrees of freedom are allowed to vary."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:131
msgid "最適化アルゴリズムと収束判定"
msgstr "Optimization Algorithms and Convergence Criteria"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:133
msgid ""
"最適化アルゴリズムは、エネルギーとその勾配をもとに次の構造を選ぶ。 BFGSなどの準Newton法では、位置を動かしたときの勾配の変化を使って、 "
"エネルギーの曲率を表す行列やその逆行列の近似を更新する。 曲率が大きい方向と小さい方向で変位の大きさを変えられるため、 "
"全方向に同じ尺度で進むより効率よく極小に近づける場合がある [OptFletcher1970]_。"
msgstr ""
"An optimization algorithm uses the energy and its gradient to select the "
"next structure. Quasi-Newton methods such as BFGS use the change in the "
"gradient after a displacement to update an approximation to the energy "
"curvature matrix or the inverse of that matrix. Since step sizes can "
"differ between directions of high and low curvature, these methods can "
"reach a minimum more efficiently than using the same scale in all "
"directions [OptFletcher1970]_."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:139
msgid ""
"原子緩和は、動かせる方向の残留力が設定した許容値に入ったかで判断する。 可変セルでは、許された変形に対応する応力と外圧の差も見る。 "
"エネルギーの変化が小さくても、更新幅が小さいだけなら力や応力は残る。 電子状態の収束誤差や\\ :ref:`基底の打ち切り<basis-set-"
"cutoff>`\\ でも 力や応力は変わりうるため、比較に必要な精度まで数値条件を収束させる。"
msgstr ""
"Judge atomic relaxation by whether residual forces along the allowed "
"directions fall within the specified tolerance. For variable-cell "
"optimization, also check the mismatch between the stress corresponding to"
" the allowed deformations and the external pressure. Even if the energy "
"change is small, forces or stress remain if the change is small only "
"because the step is small. Incomplete convergence of the electronic "
"structure and \\ :ref:`basis-set truncation <basis-set-cutoff>`\\  can "
"also change the forces and stress, so converge the numerical settings to "
"the accuracy needed for the comparison."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:145
msgid ""
"力が消えた構造は、指定した自由度についての停留点である。 拘束を解くと、元の計算では動かせなかった方向にエネルギーが下がることがある。 "
"高対称構造では力が対称性で打ち消し合うこともあるため、\\ :ref:`動的安定性<imaginary-frequency>`\\ "
"まで調べるには、 原子変位に対するエネルギー曲率をフォノンなどで調べる。"
msgstr ""
"A structure with vanishing forces is a stationary point with respect to "
"the specified degrees of freedom. Lifting a constraint can reveal an "
"energy decrease along a direction that was fixed in the original "
"calculation. In high-symmetry structures, symmetry can cancel the forces,"
" so to assess \\ :ref:`dynamical stability <imaginary-frequency>`\\  as "
"well, examine the energy curvature with respect to atomic displacements, "
"for example using phonons."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:153
msgid "説明用の事例：力が消えてもセルに応力が残る場合"
msgstr "Worked Example: Residual Cell Stress at Zero Force"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:155
msgid ""
"固定セルで原子に働く力が消えても、セルを動かす余地は残る。 変位を :math:`x`、基準体積を :math:`V_0`、相対的な体積変化を "
":math:`\\eta=(V-V_0)/V_0` とする。体積を変えると 原子が落ち着く位置もずれる模型を考える。"
msgstr ""
"Even when the forces on the atoms vanish in a fixed cell, further cell "
"relaxation is still possible. Let :math:`x` be the displacement, "
":math:`V_0` the reference volume, and :math:`\\eta=(V-V_0)/V_0` the "
"relative volume change. Consider a model in which changing the volume "
"shifts the equilibrium position of the atom."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:160
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"E(x,\\eta)=\\frac{k}{2}(x-x_0-\\lambda\\eta)^2\n"
"    +\\frac{BV_0}{2}(\\eta-\\eta_0)^2."
msgstr ""
"E(x,\\eta)=\\frac{k}{2}(x-x_0-\\lambda\\eta)^2\n"
"    +\\frac{BV_0}{2}(\\eta-\\eta_0)^2."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:166
msgid ""
":math:`k` は原子変位の曲率、:math:`B` は体積変化に対する剛性を表す パラメータである。:math:`x_0` "
"は基準体積での平衡位置、 :math:`\\lambda` は体積の変化と原子位置を結びつける係数、 :math:`\\eta_0` "
"はエネルギーが最小になる体積変化である。"
msgstr ""
"The parameters :math:`k` and :math:`B` represent the curvature with "
"respect to atomic displacement and the stiffness against volume changes, "
"respectively. The parameter :math:`x_0` is the equilibrium position at "
"the reference volume, :math:`\\lambda` couples the volume change to the "
"atomic position, and :math:`\\eta_0` is the volume change that minimizes "
"the energy."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:171
msgid ""
":math:`V=V_0` に固定すると\\ :eq:`structure-force-variation`\\ から "
":math:`F=-k(x-x_0)` なので、緩和後は :math:`x=x_0` となる。 この点では\\ :eq:`structure-"
"coupled-cell-model`\\ の第1項はゼロになる。 第2項を :math:`V` "
"で微分すると、:math:`d\\eta/dV=1/V_0` なので :math:`dE/dV=B(\\eta-\\eta_0)` "
"となる。等方変形では :eq:`structure-stress-variation`\\ の2式から、:math:`dE/dV` は "
"引張を正とした各対角応力に等しい。固定セルの緩和後に残る対角応力は :math:`-B\\eta_0` である。"
msgstr ""
"At fixed :math:`V=V_0`, Equation \\ :eq:`structure-force-variation`\\  "
"gives :math:`F=-k(x-x_0)`, so relaxation gives :math:`x=x_0`. The first "
"term in Equation \\ :eq:`structure-coupled-cell-model`\\  vanishes there."
" Differentiating the second term with respect to :math:`V` and using "
":math:`d\\eta/dV=1/V_0` gives :math:`dE/dV=B(\\eta-\\eta_0)`. For an "
"isotropic deformation, the two expressions in Equation :eq:`structure-"
"stress-variation`\\  show that :math:`dE/dV` equals each diagonal stress "
"component in the tension-positive convention. The diagonal stress "
"remaining after fixed-cell relaxation is :math:`-B\\eta_0`."

