msgid ""
"表では :math:`V_0=100\\,\\text{Å}^3`、:math:`B=1\\,\\mathrm{eV}/\\text{Å}^3`、"
" :math:`k=2\\,\\mathrm{eV}/\\text{Å}^2`、:math:`x_0=0.10\\,\\text{Å}`、 "
":math:`\\lambda=1.0\\,\\text{Å}`、:math:`\\eta_0=0.02` とした。 外圧ゼロでは\\ :eq"
":`structure-enthalpy-variation`\\ により応力ゼロが "
"体積が自由な場合の条件となる。:math:`\\eta=\\eta_0` まで変形させれば、 原子の平衡位置も "
":math:`x_0+\\lambda\\eta_0=0.12\\,\\text{Å}` に変わる。"
msgstr ""
"The table uses :math:`V_0=100\\,\\text{Å}^3`, "
":math:`B=1\\,\\mathrm{eV}/\\text{Å}^3`, "
":math:`k=2\\,\\mathrm{eV}/\\text{Å}^2`, :math:`x_0=0.10\\,\\text{Å}`, "
":math:`\\lambda=1.0\\,\\text{Å}`, and :math:`\\eta_0=0.02`. At zero "
"external pressure, Equation \\ :eq:`structure-enthalpy-variation`\\  "
"gives zero stress as the condition when the volume is free. Allowing the "
"cell to deform to :math:`\\eta=\\eta_0` also shifts the equilibrium "
"atomic position to :math:`x_0+\\lambda\\eta_0=0.12\\,\\text{Å}`."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:210
msgid "説明用の事例：曲率の違いと最適化の進み方"
msgstr "Worked Example: How Curvature Affects Optimization"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:212
msgid "曲率が方向によって大きく異なると、最急降下法は狭い谷をジグザグに横切る。 二つの無次元座標を :math:`p,q` とし、無次元のエネルギーを"
msgstr ""
"When the curvature differs greatly by direction, steepest descent zigzags"
" across a narrow valley. Let the two dimensionless coordinates be "
":math:`p,q` and the dimensionless energy be given by"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:215
#, python-brace-format
msgid "e(p,q)=\\frac{p^2+100q^2}{2}"
msgstr "e(p,q)=\\frac{p^2+100q^2}{2}"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:220
msgid ""
"とする。初期点 :math:`(1,0.01)` では、勾配 :math:`\\boldsymbol g=(p,100q)` "
"の2成分は同じ1である。最急降下法では :math:`-\\boldsymbol g` 方向に進み、その直線上の極小を選ぶ。 座標を "
":math:`\\boldsymbol x=(p,q)` とする。方向 :math:`\\boldsymbol d` に進むときのステップは、 "
":math:`e(\\boldsymbol x+\\alpha\\boldsymbol d)` を :math:`\\alpha` "
"で微分してゼロとおくと得られる。"
msgstr ""
"At the starting point :math:`(1,0.01)`, both components of the gradient "
":math:`\\boldsymbol g=(p,100q)` equal 1. Steepest descent moves in the "
"direction :math:`-\\boldsymbol g` and selects the minimum on that line. "
"Write the coordinates as :math:`\\boldsymbol x=(p,q)`. For a step in "
"direction :math:`\\boldsymbol d`, differentiate :math:`e(\\boldsymbol "
"x+\\alpha\\boldsymbol d)` with respect to :math:`\\alpha` and set the "
"derivative to zero to obtain the step length,"

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:227
msgid ""
"\\alpha=-\\frac{\\boldsymbol g^{\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol d}\n"
"              {\\boldsymbol d^{\\mathsf T} A_{\\mathrm H}\\boldsymbol d},"
"\n"
"\\qquad A_{\\mathrm H}=\\operatorname{diag}(1,100)."
msgstr ""
"\\alpha=-\\frac{\\boldsymbol g^{\\mathsf T}\\boldsymbol d}\n"
"              {\\boldsymbol d^{\\mathsf T} A_{\\mathrm H}\\boldsymbol d},"
"\n"
"\\qquad A_{\\mathrm H}=\\operatorname{diag}(1,100)."

#: ../../electronic/structure_optimization.rst:234
msgid ""
"BFGSでも直線上の極小を求める。最初は逆Hessianの近似に単位行列を使うため、 "
"最初の方向は最急降下法と一致する。BFGSは1ステップでの位置の変化と勾配の "
"変化を使い、逆Hessianの近似を更新する。これにより2回目の探索の方向が 最急降下法と異なり、この二次形式では極小に届く。"
msgstr ""
"BFGS also finds the minimum along a line. Since it starts with the "
"identity matrix as the approximation to the inverse Hessian, its first "
"direction agrees with steepest descent. BFGS then uses the changes in "
"position and gradient over one step to update the inverse Hessian "
"approximation. The second search therefore takes a different direction "
"from steepest descent and reaches the minimum for this quadratic form."

